# Styles and ownership

**Prerequisites:** [first component](/docs/tutorials/first-component/).
**Kind:** concept.
**Next:** [CSS reference](/docs/reference/language/css/).

| Layer | Where | Collision model |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Component `@css` | Inside `@component` | Lowering stamps `data-rocci-css` and wraps rules in CSS `@scope` |
| File `@css` | Module top-level | Concatenated in source order for that file |
| Asset CSS | `[assets]` files under `/assets` | Global, ordinary CSS |

Authors keep writing `class="card"`. Document chrome belongs on `body` or
`:scope`, not `html { … }`. Patch fragments should not carry a sibling
`<style>`. `:deep` piercing is **planned**.

Preview injects styles for `rocci view`. A production pipeline can extract the
same style artifacts once.

**Related:** [Styling example](/examples/styling/).
